Why: Info.plist values are read in process instead of by a plutil process per key, so list_apps and the running-app snapshot the registry takes before each launch_app take tens of milliseconds instead of most of a second.

Listing apps reads CFBundleIdentifier, CFBundleDisplayName/CFBundleName and
LSUIElement/LSBackgroundOnly from every running and installed bundle, each
through `plutil -extract <key> raw`: hundreds of processes per list_apps.
ToolRegistry also invokes list_apps before every launch_app to tell which
process the launch started. One helper, info_plist_value, parses the file
with CFPropertyListCreateWithData and renders the value as plutil raw does
(string, true/false, number), so every caller keeps its parsing. Measured on
one Mac (release build, 85 apps): list_all_apps 0.85 s -> 0.075 s,
list_running_apps 0.33 s -> 0.06 s, output identical. Upstreamable as is.

